[I] A scrollable-tiling Wayland compositor

[T] niri is a scrollable-tiling Wayland compositor in which windows are
[T] arranged in columns on an infinite strip going to the right, so opening
[T] a new window never resizes existing ones. Each monitor has its own
[T] window strip and dynamic, vertically arranged workspaces; it also
[T] features an overview mode and a built-in screenshot UI.

[U] https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri

[A] Ivan Molodetskikh
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/x11
[F] CROSS
[R] - alpha arc avr32 blackfin cris hppa hppa64 i860 m68k microblaze nios2 openrisc superh

